.TH SEQ 1 "5th of August 2026" zenithutils "User Commands"

.SH NAME
\fBseq\fP - print a sequence of numbers

.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
\fBseq\fP \fI[-f fmt | -w] [-s sep] last\fP
\fBseq\fP \fI[-f fmt | -w] [-s sep] first last\fP
\fBseq\fP \fI[-f fmt | -w] [-s sep] first increment last\fP
.EE

.SH DESCRIPION
seq prints a sequence of numbers

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB-f fmt\fP
use fmt to tell printf how to display numbers. Incompatible with '-w'

.TP
\fB-s sep\fP
use sep as a separator between numbers. default is newline "\\n"

.TP
\fB-w\fP
pad numbers with zeroes, using the largest number of the sequence to know how many zeros to use. Incompatible with '-f'
